{"chunk_id": "cd1bb43d301c", "text": "This section recounts the controversial death of the great teacher Drona during the Kurukshetra war and the fury it awakens in his son, Aswatthaman. Suspecting deceit, Drona asks whether his son is dead. Torn between truth and the need for victory, Yudhishthira ambiguously declares that \u201cAswatthaman\u201d is slain\u2014referring to an elephant but muttering the qualifier so softly that Drona believes his son dead. Grief-stricken, Drona lays down his weapons and enters meditation on the battlefield. Despite protests from warriors and Arjuna\u2019s plea to spare their teacher, Dhrishtadyumna beheads the defenseless preceptor. When Aswatthaman hears of this, he erupts in grief and rage, condemning the deceit and swearing vengeance on the Panchalas and Yudhishthira. The episode highlights the moral breakdown of the war and sets the stage for Aswatthaman\u2019s devastating retaliation.\nYudhishthira\u2019s half-truth leads Drona to despair and death at Dhrishtadyumna\u2019s hands, provoking Aswatthaman\u2019s furious vow of revenge against the Panchalas.\nThemes: deception in war, death of Drona, revenge oath, dharma vs strategy, filial grief", "vector": [-0.010854718275368214, -0.0028467527590692043, -0.0062224287539720535, -0.00043922531767748296, 0.0018748140428215265, 0.018475256860256195, -0.045601945370435715, 0.0028585440013557673, -0.011750856414437294, -0.014594240114092827, 0.01313885860145092, 0.025630880147218704, 0.007297120057046413, 0.01076038833707571, 0.01592833921313286, 0.010423494502902031, 0.04719208553433418, -0.002012940589338541, 0.0273423008620739, -0.028191274031996727, -0.0028366458136588335, -0.008482986129820347, -0.008388656191527843, 0.039052728563547134, -0.0016490952111780643, 0.020483143627643585, 0.005804680287837982, -0.024808859452605247, 0.007337547373026609, -0.020914368331432343, -0.014958085492253304, -0.020024968311190605, -0.002230237005278468, -0.01412258855998516, -0.01893343217670917